      "text": "Hello everyone, thank you UNESCO and the AI for AI community for this opportunity. My name is Matias Carzon from Chroma data in Latin America and the Caribbean. My thesis for this presentation in one line, if you are not in the data you are not in the decision. In medicine, fairness isn't a feature, fairness is safety. Why equity equals safety in medicine? Let's talk about this. AI already influences triage, diagnosis, and care pathways. Average accuracy can look great and still leave some groups behind. We must ask, at the operating point we deploy, who is actually protected? Two concepts to hold, false negative rate, missing disease, and calibration, how predicted risk maps to real outcome in each group.",
