      "text": "There's a third problem, big problem. A big genomic gap, Latin America only accounts for 0.38% of participation in genome-wide association studies, limiting downstream precision medicine models for our population. So, if we think about this, when global models are trained on English language papers, European ancestry genomes, and imaging from well-equipped hospitals, maybe Latin American and Caribbean patients are statistically absent from that learning signal. Let's see another case. A celebrated risk model validated out of the main show only moderate performance in Mexican women, with variation by mammography vendor models. So, we can think that models don't travel well without local data and tuning, fine tuning. We need to validate on our patients and our hardware before clinical use.",
