      "text": "Also, we need to publish subgroup metrics and device-specific performance if we want to use it in Latin America and Caribbean people. So, what these two cases that we have seen teaches, there are many more cases I just gather two specific cases. It teaches that the sources of harm span measurement, sensor, imaging, objective choice, data distribution, and operations. So, average accuracy is not enough. Equity must be engineer, measure, and govern. So, what can we ask our vendor like checklist to demand from their models? So, first of all, we need them to publish a data sheet with population composition, including Hispanic, Latino, etc. Geography, device is used, and also non-gaps. We should also ask to publish a model car with metrics by subgroup, by device site,",
